domination ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\\n447: \\n448: /-- `f : V → {0,1,2}` is a Roman dominating function when every vertex labelled\\n449: `0` has a neighbour labelled `2`.\\n450: \\n451: graphcalc solves this as a MIP over binaries `x, y` with `f = x + 2y`,\\n452: constraint `x v + y v + Σ_{u ∈ N(v)} y u ≥ 1` and exclusion `x v + y v ≤ 1`;\\n453: that is exactly the condition below. -/\\n454: def IsRomanDominatingFunction (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n455:     (f : V → Fin 3) : Prop := ∀ v : V, f v = 0 → ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ f u = 2\\n456: \\n457: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (f : V → Fin 3) :\\n458:     Decidable (IsRomanDominatingFunction G f) := by\\n459:   unfold IsRomanDominatingFunction; infer_instance\\n460: \\n461: def romanWeight (f : V → Fin 3) : ℕ := ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ)\\n462: \\n463: /-- Total, not partial: the constant function `2` is always Roman dominating\\n464: (no vertex is labelled `0`), so a witness always exists. -/\\n465: def romanDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\\n466:   (((univ.filter (IsRomanDominatingFunc\\n<truncated 338 bytes>\\nr a neighbour labelled `3` or two neighbours labelled `2`, and a vertex\\n472: labelled `1` has a neighbour labelled `≥ 2`.\\n473: \\n474: The first clause is written as graphcalc's linearisation\\n475: `0.5·|N₂(v)| + |N₃(v)| ≥ 1`, but as two existentials rather than as\\n476: `Finset.card` of a filter: \\\"at least two neighbours labelled 2\\\" is \\\"two distinct\\n477: neighbours labelled 2\\\", and the kernel reduces a pair of quantifiers over `V`\\n478: far more cheaply than it builds and counts a `Finset`. Written the counting way\\n479: first, all seven order-5 checks exhausted their heartbeat budget. -/\\n480: def IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n481:     (f : V → Fin 4) : Prop :=\\n482:   (∀ v : V, f v = 0 →\\n483:       (∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ f u = 3) ∨\\n484:       (∃ u : V, ∃ w : V, u ≠ w ∧ G.Adj v u ∧ G.Adj v w ∧ f u = 2 ∧ f w = 2)) ∧\\n485:   (∀ v : V, f v = 1 → ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ 2 ≤ (f u : ℕ))\\n486: \\n487: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (f : V → Fin 4) :\\n488:     Decidable (IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction G f) := by\\n489:   unfold IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction; infer_instance\\n490: \\n491: def doubleRomanWeight (f : V → Fin 4) : ℕ := ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ)\\n492: \\n493: /-- Total, for the same reason as `romanDominationNumber`: constant `3` works. -/\\n494: def doubleRomanDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\\n495:   (((univ.filter (IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction G)).image\\n496:     doubleRomanWeight).min).getD 0\\n497: \\n498: /- ── radius ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\\n499: \\n500: /-- Vertices within `k` steps of `v`, by iterated neighbourhood expansion.\\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n17: {\"step_index\":16,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:29:26Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"537\",\"StartLine\":\"500\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View radius definitions\\\"\"}}]}\n18: {\"step_index\":17,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:29:27Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:29:27+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:29:27+02:00\\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\\nTotal Lines: 537\\nTotal Bytes: 27292\\nShowing lines 500 to 537\\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\\n500: /-- Vertices within `k` steps of `v`, by iterated neighbourhood expansion.\\n501: Distance is not available to the kernel directly (`SimpleGraph.dist` is defined\\n502: through `sInf` over walk lengths), so it is reconstructed as reachability. -/\\n503: def ballWithin (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ → V → Finset V\\n504:   | 0,       v => {v}\\n505:   | (k + 1), v =>\\n506:       let B := ballWithin G k v\\n507:       B ∪ B.biUnion (fun u => univ.filter (fun w => G.Adj u w))\\n508: \\n509: /-- Eccentricity of `v`: least `k` with every vertex within `k` steps. -/\\n510: def eccentricity (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) : ℕ :=\\n511:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V) (fun k => ballWithin G k v = univ)\\n512: \\n513: def radius (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\\n514:   ((univ.image (eccentricity G)).min).getD 0\\n515: \\n516: /-- Undefined on a disconnected graph, where some vertex never reaches all of\\n517: `univ` and `minUpTo` would fall back to `n`. networkx raises there. -/\\n518: def HasRadius (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\\n519:   ∀ v : V, ballWithin G (Fintype.card V) v = univ\\n520: \\n521: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\\n522:     Decidable (HasRadius G) := by unfold HasRadius; infer_instance\\n523: \\n524: /- ── graph construction from an explicit edge list ────────────────────────── -/\\n525: \\n526: /-- The graph on `Fin n` with the given edge list, symmetrised and loop-free.\\n527: This is the shape the disproof exporter emits for a refuting witness.\\n528: \\n529: `SimpleGraph.fromRel` supplies the symmetry and irreflexivity proofs, so this\\n530: stays a definition rather than a bundle of obligations that would have to be\\n531: re-discharged (and re-adjusted across mathlib versions) in generated code. It is\\n532: an `abbrev` so that `DecidableRel` synthesis can see through it at the use site. -/\\n533: abbrev ofEdges (n : ℕ) (es : List (Fin n × Fin n)) : SimpleGraph (Fin n) :=\\n534:   SimpleGraph.fromRel (fun u v => (u, v) ∈ es)\\n535: \\n536: end GraphCalc\\n537: \\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\\n\"}\n19: {\"step_index\":18,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:29:27Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View first 100 lines of GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\\\"\"}}]}\n20: {\"step_index\":19,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:29:28Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:29:28+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:29:28+02:00\\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\\nTotal Lines: 537\\nTotal Bytes: 27292\\nShowing lines 1 to 100\\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\\n1: /-\\n2: GraphInvariantsComputable.lean — a *computable* mirror of the invariants in\\n3: `GraphInvariants.lean`, so that a claim about one explicit finite graph can be\\n4: settled by `decide` rather than by a hand proof.\\n5: \\n6: Why this file exists\\n7: --------------------\\n8: `GraphInvariants.lean` defines the invariants the way a mathematician states\\n9: them: `dominationNumber G = sInf { n | ∃ s, s.card = n ∧ G.IsDominatingSet s }`.\\n10: That is the right *specification*, but `sInf` over a `Set ℕ` (under\\n11: `open scoped Classical`) is **noncomputable**, so the kernel cannot evaluate it\\n12: on a concrete graph — measured directly, `decide` succeeds on `order`, `size`\\n13: and `minDegree`, and fails on every `sInf`/`sSup` invariant (domination,\\n14: annihilation, the zero-forcing family, and mathlib's own `indepNum`/`cliqueNum`).\\n15: \\n16: That blocks the cheapest source of formal results we have. The refutation engine\\n17: kills thousands of candidates and knows exactly which graph kills each one; each\\n18: such pair is a `¬∀ …` theorem whose proof is \\\"evaluate both sides on this graph\\\"\\n19: — but only if the invariants actually evaluate.\\n20: \\n21: The definitions here are the same mathematical objects expressed as a minimum\\n22: over an explicitly enumerated `Finset`, which the kernel *can* reduce. They are\\n23: deliberately kept in their own namespace: nothing in the existing proof pipeline\\n24: changes, and `GraphInvariants.lean` remains the specification of record.\\n25: -/\\n26: import Mathlib\\n27: \\n<truncated 2085 bytes>\\nleGraph V) : ℕ := Fintype.card V\\n68: \\n69: def size (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ := G.edgeFinset.card\\n70: \\n71: /- ── independence / clique ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\\n72: \\n73: /-- `s` is independent: no two of its vertices are adjacent. -/\\n74: def IsIndependentFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\\n75:   ∀ u ∈ s, ∀ w ∈ s, ¬ G.Adj u w\\n76: \\n77: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\\n78:     Decidable (IsIndependentFinset G s) := by\\n79:   unfold IsIndependentFinset; infer_instance\\n80: \\n81: /-- Independence number: the largest independent set. -/\\n82: def indepNum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\\n83:   (((univ.powerset.filter (IsIndependentFinset G)).image Finset.card).max).getD 0\\n84: \\n85: /-- `s` is a clique: distinct vertices of `s` are pairwise adjacent. -/\\n86: def IsCliqueFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\\n87:   ∀ u ∈ s, ∀ w ∈ s, u ≠ w → G.Adj u w\\n88: \\n89: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\\n90:     Decidable (IsCliqueFinset G s) := by\\n91:   unfold IsCliqueFinset; infer_instance\\n92: \\n93: /-- Clique number: the largest clique. -/\\n94: def cliqueNum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\\n95:   (((univ.powerset.filter (IsCliqueFinset G)).image Finset.card).max).getD 0\\n96: \\n97: /- ── domination family ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\\n98: \\n99: def IsDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\\n100:   ∀ v : V, v ∈ s ∨ ∃ w ∈ s, G.Adj v w\\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n21: {\"step_index\":20,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:29:28Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"grep_search\",\"args\":{\"MatchPerLine\":\"true\",\"Query\":\"\\\"IsNontrivialClass\\\"\",\"SearchPath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search IsNontrivialClass\\\"\"}}]}\n22: {\"step_index\":21,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:29:29Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:29:29+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:29:29+02:00\\n{\\\"File\\\":\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\\\",\\\"LineNumber\\\":272,\\\"LineContent\\\":\\\"def IsNontrivialClass (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop := 2 ≤ order G\\\"}\\n{\\\"File\\\":\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\\\",\\\"LineNumber\\\":274,\\\"LineContent\\\":\\\"instance (G : SimpleGraph V) : Decidable (IsNontrivialClass G) := by\\\"}\\n{\\\"File\\\":\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\\\",\\\"LineNumber\\\":275,\\\"LineContent\\\":\\\"  unfold IsNontrivialClass; infer_instance\\\"}\"}\n23: {\"step_index\":22,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:29:29Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View check.sh script\\\"\"}}]}\n24: {\"step_index\":23,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:29:31Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:29:31+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:29:31+02:00\\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh`\\nTotal Lines: 51\\nTotal Bytes: 2182\\nShowing lines 1 to 51\\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\\n1: #!/bin/bash\\n2: # check.sh — the ONLY command an agent may run.\\n3: #\\n4: #   /abs/path/tools/antigravity/check.sh FILE.lean\\n5: #\\n6: # Lives outside every agent workspace and is hashed by guard.sh: agents can\\n7: # write inside their workspace, so a checker kept there could be rewritten into\\n8: # anything. It screens the file first (tools/antigravity_handoff.py lint), because\\n9: # Lean elaboration can itself run shell commands; then elaborates it with bare\\n10: # `lean` and an explicit LEAN_PATH, and prints every theorem's axioms. Nothing\\n11: # here depends on $HOME — agents run under a private one — and `lake` is never\\n12: # involved (in this project lake deletes Mathlib when it cannot re-clone).\\n13: set -uo pipefail\\n14: f=\\\"${1:?usage: check.sh FILE.lean}\\\"\\n15: [ -f \\\"$f\\\" ] || { echo \\\"CHECK: no such file: $f\\\"; exit 2; }\\n16: \\n17: ROOT=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$(readlink -f \\\"$0\\\")\\\")/../..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\n18: # Tool paths come from a protected file, not from the home directory: agents run\\n19: # under a private HOME, and on compute nodes `getent passwd` reports a different\\n20: # home (/home/<user>@ad…) than the one the tools live in.\\n21: ENVF=\\\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_env\\\"\\n22: export ELAN_HOME=\\\"$(grep -m1 '^AGF_ELAN_HOME=' \\\"$ENVF\\\" 2>/dev/null | cut -d= -f2-)\\\"\\n23: LEAN=\\\"$ELAN_HOME/bin/lean\\\"\\n24: [ -x \\\"$LEAN\\\" ] || { echo \\\"CHECK: lean not found (ELAN_HOME='$ELAN_HOME' from $ENVF)\\\"; exit 2; }\\n25: PY=\\\"$ROOT/.venv/bin/python\\\"\\n26: LP_FILE=\\\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_lean_path\\\"\\n27: [ -s \\\"$LP_FILE\\\" ] || { echo \\\"CHECK: missing $LP_FILE\\\"; exit 2; }\\n28: export LEAN_PATH=\\\"$(cat \\\"$LP_FILE\\\")\\\"\\n29: \\n30: orig=\\\"$(ls \\\"$ROOT\\\"/benchmark/challenges_*/\\\"$(basename \\\"$f\\\")\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -1)\\\"\\n31: if ! \\\"$PY\\\" \\\"$ROOT/tools/antigravity_handoff.py\\\" lint ${orig:+--original \\\"$orig\\\"} \\\"$f\\\"; then\\n32:   echo \\\"CHECK: refused to elaborate — remove the construct named above.\\\"\\n33:   exit 3\\n34: fi\\n3